Round 582: the Stadium Tycoon league, at the hook's cadence (dt 0.2s)
1) Promoted if and only if champion
   55 titles and 55 promotions across 96 seasons; 41 seasons finished below the top and none of those went up
2) Table integrity
   60 matchday tables checked: every club played every matchday, points are 3W+D, goals balance, your row matches your match events
3) Strength decides the title
   title rate squad 30 100%, squad 0 15% (gap 0.85); neutral arm 18% vs 15% (gap 0.02)
4) Pace against the first Sell up and the old ladder
   median first promotion 10.50 min against first Sell up 13.37 min (promotion first in 10/10); before the league: 14.7 and 13.44
5) No reroll across a reload
   6 seasons reloaded mid-match finished with tables identical to the runs that never reloaded
6) Migration from V1 saves
   251 V1 saves from 0 to 250 home wins loaded into the division their win count reached, everything else as V1 loads it, and each loads back in V1 with its league
7) Names
   1470 leagues across 21 reps, 10 divisions and 7 seasons: names unique, short enough, from the bank, never one of 483 real clubs; the picker never offers a taken name
8) Rebuild still plays the shared calendar
   rebuildDeck imports the shared calendar, leagueCore imports nothing, 4 of 4 Rebuild harnesses green
9) No wall: a club that can compete gets promoted in time
   never promoted in three hours: squad 3 0/30, squad 6 0/30; median first promotion 21.0 and 21.0 min
10) The loader keeps divisions, refuses doctored leagues, and ties go your way
   a division 6 league reloads exactly, keeps its division with a bad field, a doctored Summit loads at the career best, an impossible table is refused, a kept name sticks, a dead heat goes your way

